From fd59900cb7384a49ab5cf9830e36c1059fd035f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:24:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] Noah-MP combine: keep snow sensible heat when layers
 merge or vanish

Three energy leaks in combine (both modules):
- a thin layer merged by mass keeps the receiver's temperature;
- snow that stops being layered drops its layers' sensible heat;
- truncated bulk snow changes the top soil layer's ice at that layer's
  temperature without its heat.

Merge and hand over the sensible heat with the heat capacities csnow uses
(per mass) and the top soil layer's heat capacity, as thermoprop.

Measured (C96 control_p8_ugwpv1, 24 h, with the csnow and combo fixes):
Noah-MP soil energy residual 3.9e-4 -> 4.3e-8 W/m2, all of it at step 1
(the initial state). With them and the combine-count fix: T rms 0.147 K;
land fields at noise.

Part of a water-conservation project for UFS physics (NOAA GML / CIRES).

AI-assisted: written with Claude Opus 5.5; reviewed by author
